64;d=json.load(sys.stdin);t=base64.b64decode(d['content_base64']).decode();print(len(t));import re\nfor l in t.splitlines():\n    if re.search(r'experiment|E8|finite|analysis',l,re.I):print(l[:300])\""], ["description", "Read story reply and Outline mentions"]], "output": "```console\n[]\n\n36798\n# Outline (story-repo, revision 14 (finite-population account of the disjoint-draw overcoverage tested; answers experiment-repo story-repo#10); revision 13 (alphafold T2 reference cell final: 4 of 4 T2 sets no gain; 55 headline rows); revision 12 (the neither-valid case of the baseline rule stated a\nBuilt from the objective, the idea's `Brief` (rev. 4) and `prior_work.md`. It says what to test and what each part of the paper must say. It does **not** fix any result: every claim below is a hypothesis with a stated way to fail, and the paper reports whichever outcome the experiments give.\n**Headline measure and margin (set now; analysis may not move it after seeing results).** Paired width ratio r = width(arm)/width(A2 PPI++) on the same draws, with 95% CI over repetitions. Per cell: **no gain** if the CI of r lies inside [0.98, 1.02]; **gain** if the CI upper bound < 0.95 and the ar\n**n-grid and N.** Log-spaced n ∈ {30, 100, 300, 1000, 3000, 10000} restricted to what each pool allows (iid with replacement from the pool as population, or n+N ≪ pool, documented per set), plus one *reference n* per set fixed before the runs (the labeled-set size for ballots; for the other sets a v\n**Compute plan (planning estimate, to be replaced by measurement).** Target total ≲ 8 CPU-h (`resources.md` estimate; one week). Allocation as a starting point: 1-D arms (A0–A7) on all nine sets ≲ 3 CPU-h (isotonic fit on n labels + prediction on capped N is ms-scale; the 380k-record census/plankton\n**Data access and fallback.** First job of analysis: download all nine ppi-python sets in the container. If Google Drive/gdown is blocked, tell story and idea at once; the fallback is folktables / sklearn data with a **fixed predictor trained on a split disjoint from the labeled/unlabeled draws** an\n5. **Experimental design.** Datasets (9 sets, per-set pool/replacement scheme; ballots and plankton truth caveats), arms on equal terms (T1/T2), validity protocol and win rule (fixed in advance), MC reps, synthetic suite.\n## 4. Experiments (for analysis; the question each answers, not the method)\n- **E9 The clip (C8).** The ladder gets a \"clip\" step between PPI and unclipped PPI++ (Brief rev. 8), reported per set and n; the clip term (1/n − 1/M)(b\\* − c)²Var(f) is computed per dataset and n and compared with the measured width gap. Synthetic sweep over the slope b with the known variance for\n- **E8 Optional, last:** regression-coefficient extension only (selection of g is in E3/E4).\n- **Data access:** see section 1 (first job of analysis; fixed predictor on a disjoint split if the fallback is used).\n- **Claim-evidence gate:** a claim goes into the paper only with its experiment run to the validity protocol; a cell where a method is invalid is reported as invalid, not dropped. If E3 shows no headroom on the real sets, C2 becomes \"PPI++ is near the floor\" and C3/C7 carry the novelty; if C1 formul\n- **Assumption check:** the pooled-Z/MCAR statements rely on iid-with-replacement pool sampling; analysis confirms the design before reporting.\n- analysis (`experiment-repo`): E1–E8 and the validity of each result; tells story which claims the results carry or not.\n## 8. Story as the first complete pass of results stands (story-repo#6; measurements are analysis's; T2/B5 headline rows and the disjoint-draw cells were still running)\n- The overcoverage of the disjoint-draw cells (galaxies, coverage 0.984 at n = 3000) is explained by the finite pool: tested in `finite_pop_check.csv` (revision 14). The SD of the PPI++ estimate falls relative to the iid cell as M/P grows (galaxies n = 3000: 0.828 observed, 0.831 from an approximati\n**Revision 11 (E9, strongest-valid baseline, break-even by curve; `results/` at experiment-repo 19eb276; measurements are analysis's).**\n- **gene_expression attribution, final split** (analysis): at n = 100 the SD ratio to the package is 0.890 with λ fixed at λ\\*, 0.896 pooled linear, 0.895 in-sample OLS, and SE/SD is 0.974 for the\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "4848adec-6031-5aca-967d-1c35b4cb484f", "at": 1795690966.909592, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 74913, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "4284227db8c6d52342fa9407b0534f26", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "b9c49b49-2c60-5852-bba2-9beb28ed5d85", "at": 1795690966.918005, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 74914, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "4284227db8c6d52342fa9407b0534f26", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "18ba8c98-1c77-5d34-9f0e-ce4ed5b0a12f", "at": 1795690966.927744, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 74915, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "4284227db8c6d52342fa9407b0534f26", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "aca4f959-de75-5307-aadd-921afe99196f", "at": 1795690967.0951107, "until": 1795690967.1649814, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 74917, "layer": "worker", "category": "collaborate", "kind": "collaboration.request", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "exe